hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"28","On garments. Amr ibn Uthman narrated to us, Isma'il - meaning Ibn Ayyash - narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Yahya ibn Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three whose prayer does not rise above their heads - and he mentioned the hadith - he said: And a woman who stands for prayer with her ear exposed."
"29","Hannad narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Abu al-Umayys, from Awn ibn Abdullah, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood for prayer, nothing pleased him but clean garments and sweet fragrance."
